      { type: "p", text: "Participate in class to improve communication. Use time management to complete important tasks on time. Problem-solving skills help handle tough work situations. Teamwork and sharing knowledge build strong collaboration. Strong skills help students succeed during future interviews." },
      { type: "h3", text: "Gain Practical Experience" },
      { type: "p", text: "Practical experience prepares students for future jobs before graduation. It helps students understand real workplace duties every day. Internships give students useful experience through practical learning. Part-time employment also helps develop confidence and skills related to the workplace. Volunteering builds responsibility. Say yes to every university learning opportunity. Real situations enhance classroom learning in practical work. Employers will sometimes favor graduates who have some work experience." },
      { type: "image", src: "/articles/best-career-planning-tips-for-university-students-2.webp" },
      { type: "p", text: "Every project builds confidence for future career success. Real experience prepares students for workplace challenges." },
      { type: "p", text: "Classrooms may not always offer the experience of practice that is needed. Students learn about how to behave at work by looking at what they do every day and by using real situations they might face. Every new task improves confidence and practical understanding. Real experience helps students prepare for future careers. Learning by doing creates lasting professional skills." },
      { type: "h2", text: "Preparing to Enter the Job Market" },
      { type: "h3", text: "Create Professional Networks" },
      { type: "p", text: "Students develop solid career opportunities later with the help of professional networks. Students should regularly meet with their teacher mentor(s) and industry experts. Career events enable students to meet with professionals of experience. Positive impressions are created (and remembered) with good communication in every meeting. Future job opportunities can be created through strong networks." },
      { type: "p", text: "All students must remain courteous in all professional interactions. It demonstrates interest and a learning attitude by asking thoughtful questions. It is important for students to stay connected to ensure that they are able to receive helpful career advice. Internships and jobs can come from good relationships. Long-term career growth is aided by professional networking." },
      { type: "p", text: "Building professional relationships takes time and regular communication. Students should stay connected with helpful mentors after university events. Good networking creates trust through honest and respectful conversations. Strong connections often provide valuable career advice. Professional relationships support future career growth." },
      { type: "h3", text: "Prepare a Strong Resume" },
      { type: "p", text: "Students are more likely to impress with their qualifications and a strong resume. Employers scan resumes prior to calling in candidates for an interview. Education skills projects and work experience should be included in students' resumes. Trust is built in every hiring process, with honest information. A resume update is beneficial to future job opportunities." },
      { type: "p", text: "Check your resume before every application. Proper spelling and clear organization make a great first impression. New achievements should be added to the update of the resume. Career planning is successful with strong resumes." },
      { type: "p", text: "Students should update resumes after every important achievement. New projects make resumes stronger and more impressive. Certificates also improve professional credibility during job applications. Every update reflects personal growth and continuous learning. A complete resume attracts greater employer attention." },
      { type: "h2", text: "Sustaining Career Growth" },
      { type: "h3", text: "Continue Learning After Graduation" },
      { type: "p", text: "Education shouldn't stop with any of the university degrees. Continuous growth and improvement are the keys to professional development. As much as possible, students will attend workshops. Professional books help to advance the knowledge of many professions. Learning is an ongoing process and foundation for future success. It is important to encourage pupils to be confident each day with new ideas." },
      { type: "image", src: "/articles/best-career-planning-tips-for-university-students-3.webp" },
      { type: "p", text: "All learning experiences build up stronger professional skills. Patience and steady improvement guarantee success in a career. Professional skills are kept alive for years with lifelong learning. Builds confidence for future challenges through daily learning." },
      { type: "p", text: "Learning should become a lifelong habit for every student. New skills improve confidence during changing workplace situations. Students should follow industry trends through trusted learning resources. Learning regularly helps keep professional knowledge up to date each year.Keeping skills improved leads to better career chances in the future." },
      { type: "h2", text: "Conclusion" },
      { type: "p", text: "Career planning allows students to build successful careers with confidence. Students understand how to make career decisions with clear goals. Students are ready for the workplace through practical experience. Good capabilities and connections lead to better jobs. The planning that is smart now is a success in the long run." },
      { type: "p", text: "Patience, dedication, and growth lead to career success. Revisit your goals every school year. Little efforts, big results in the professional field. Small positive steps lead to increased confidence for future success. Smart career planning opens up brighter opportunities for each university student." }
